  {
    "id": "CVE-2024-7535",
    "issues": [
      "352690885"
    ],
    "impacts": [
      "Inappropriate implementation in V8 in Google Chrome prior to 127.0.6533.99 allowed a remote attacker to potentially exploit heap corruption via a crafted HTML page. Reporter-observed symptom: `Fatal error in ../../src/interpreter/interpreter.cc, line 241 # Bytecode mismatch at offset 8`. Root cause: `Scope::GetHomeObjectScope` was an outward scope walk whose tolerances (arrow functions, `private_name_lookup_skips_outer_class`) let the two compiles of the same JavaScript method resolve a `super.x` reference to different home-object scopes. The resulting bytecode differs byte-for-byte between first compile and lazy recompile. The debug-only `CheckAndPrintBytecodeMismatch` fires at `interpreter.cc:241`; release builds silently install the divergent BA on the SFI while prior consumers still hold offsets against the old BA."
    ],
    "itw": false,
    "commits": [
      "https://chromium.googlesource.com/v8/v8/+/f0a3073d941249ba790a8a4bc891e82ec83e8986"
